   "attrsRaw": "class=\"slide custom-slide\" id=\"custom-1789145248336-tjyjl\"",
   "contentHtml": "<p class=\"lead al-gauche\" style=\"max-width: 1271.61px; width: 1271.61px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); left: 18.788%; top: 22.5%;\" data-pose=\"\" data-off-x=\"187.88\" data-off-y=\"225\"><span class=\"t-fr\">* Andreotta, M., Boschetti, F., Farrell, S., Paris, C., Walker, I., &amp; Hurlstone, M. J. (2026). *Do weather-related extreme events influence climate-related opinions? The case of the 2019–2020 Australian Black Summer bushfires.* [https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.251450](https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.251450)<br>* Chavalarias, D., Bouchaud, P., Chomel, V., &amp; Panahi, M. (2023). *Les nouveaux fronts du dénialisme et du climato-scepticisme : Deux années d’échanges Twitter passées aux macroscopes.r<br>* Handley, G. B. (2019). *Climate scepticism and Christian conservatism in the United States.* [https://doi.org/10.5040/9781350057050.ch-004](https://doi.org/10.5040/9781350057050.ch-004)<br>* Hornsey, M. J., &amp; Lewandowsky, S. (2022). *A toolkit for understanding and addressing climate scepticism.* [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-022-01463-y](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41562-022-01463-y)<br>* Nicolosi, E., Medina, R., Brewer, S., Vorkink, M., &amp; Allred, A. (2025). *The new denial: Climate solution misinformation on social media.* [https://doi.org/10.1017/sus.2025.10016](https://doi.org/10.1017/sus.2025.10016)<br>* Stoetzer, L. S., &amp; Zimmermann, F. (2024). *A representative survey experiment of motivated climate change denial.* [https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-023-01910-2](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-023-01910-2)<br>* Uscinski, J. E., &amp; Olivella, S. (2017). *The conditional effect of conspiracy thinking on attitudes toward climate change.* [https://doi.org/10.1177/2053168017743105](https://doi.org/10.1177/2053168017743105)<br>* Vlasceanu, M., Doell, K. C., Bak-Coleman, J. B., et al. (2024). *Addressing climate change with behavioral science: A global intervention tournament in 63 countries.* [https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adj5778](https://doi.org/10.1126/sciadv.adj5778)<br>* Wullenkord, M. C. (2022). *From denial of facts to rationalization and avoidance: Ideology, needs, and gender predict the spectrum of climate denial.* [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.paid.2022.111616](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.paid.2022.111616)</span><span class=\"t-en\" hidden=\"\"></span></p><p class=\"lead taille-xl\" data-pose=\"\" data-off-x=\"473.48\" data-off-y=\"137.88\" style=\"left: 47.348%; top: 13.788%; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><span class=\"t-fr\">Bibliographie</span><span class=\"t-en\" hidden=\"\"></span></p>"
