   "kind": "simple",
   "attrsRaw": "class=\"slide\" id=\"nv2-fox-titre\"",
   "contentHtml": "\n    <div class=\"imgcard\" data-pose=\"\" data-off-x=\"104.26\" data-off-y=\"146\" style=\"left:10.426%;top:14.6%;width:79.149%;max-width:none\"><img src=\"../medias/images/masni-fox-vaccins-1.png\" alt=\"Fox News : « Should you get the COVID and flu vaccines at the same time? »\" loading=\"lazy\"></div>\n    <p class=\"lead\" data-pose=\"\" data-off-x=\"173.01\" data-off-y=\"601.7\" style=\"left:17.301%;top:60.17%;width:56.343%;max-width:none;font-size:30px;text-align:left;\"><span class=\"t-fr\"><b>« Devriez-vous recevoir les vaccins contre la COVID et la grippe en même temps ? »</b><br><i>De nouvelles recherches suggèrent qu’il pourrait être bénéfique de les faire ensemble, mais certains médecins appellent à la prudence.</i></span><span class=\"t-en\" hidden=\"\"><b>“Should you get the COVID and flu vaccines at the same time?”</b><br><i>New research suggests it may be beneficial to double up, but some doctors urge caution.</i></span></p>\n  "
